2026-06-29 12:02:09,361 | AGENT | TechnicalArchitect Agent answered: Based on the company context, I propose an architecture that leverages our expertise in AI/ML systems, Cloud architecture, API integration, Data engineering, and Cybersecurity. 

To meet the client's requirements, we will design a solution using our existing technical stack, including our experience with cloud providers such as OVHcloud, Scaleway, and Outscale (SecNumCloud), which can provide the necessary sovereignty and security for hosting the solution.

The proposed architecture will utilize containerization using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) to ensure scalability, flexibility, and high availability. Our monitoring tools, including Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack, will be used to monitor the system's performance and ensure that it meets the required time of response and availability.

To integrate with existing systems such as business software and electronic management of documents, we will use API gateways like Kong or Apigee to securely expose APIs and manage traffic. Our experience with message brokers like Apache Kafka and RabbitMQ will help us design a robust and scalable messaging system.

For the AI/ML component, we can utilize our expertise in LLM models such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, and Falcon, and leverage our knowledge of RAG frameworks like LangChain, LlamaIndex, and Haystack. We will also use vector databases like Qdrant, Weaviate, or pgvector to efficiently store and query large amounts of data.

To ensure the solution meets the required time of response, we will optimize our inference servers using vLLM, Ollama, or TGI (Hugging Face) and apply fine-tuning methods like LoRA, QLoRA, or Full fine-tune. Our explainability tools, including SHAP, LIME, chain-of-thought prompting, and RAG source citation, will provide transparency into the decision-making process.

In terms of performance benchmarks, our typical performance is a p95 response time of 1800 ms, which is higher than the required 2 seconds. However, we can optimize our system to meet this requirement by leveraging our experience with quantisation methods like INT8 and INT4 (GPTQ), which have achieved an energy reduction of 35% in our previous projects.

To guarantee a high level of availability, we will design the system with auto-scaling capabilities to ensure that it can handle changes in workload. Our sovereign hosting options, including OVHcloud and Scaleway, which are ISO 14001 certified and use 100% renewable energy, respectively, will help minimize the environmental impact of the solution.

Overall, the proposed architecture will meet the client's requirements for response time, availability, integration with existing systems, and API interfaces while ensuring sovereignty, security, and sustainability.
