Regarding GDPR compliance, having a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and reachable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it ensures we have a dedicated point of contact for data protection issues. Our standard data residency policy is to store data within the EU only, which aligns with the client's requirement for no data transfer outside the European Union.

For protecting sensitive data, our use of anonymisation tools such as Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom Named Entity Recognition (NER) models can ensure that personal data is adequately protected. We also have experience in implementing data subject rights, including access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection, further ensuring GDPR compliance.

Our AI security controls include prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation (where inference API is the only point of access for end-users), and model update security review. These measures ensure that our AI solutions are secure and less vulnerable to data breaches or unauthorized access.

